(2) THE SUPPORT DECOMPOSITION (the k-fold folded identity)
    mu = sum_S (2lam)^(k-|S|) delta(S),  delta(empty)=1, delta(single)=0
    k=3:  mu = (2lam)^3 + 2lam*[d12+d13+d23] + d123
    (2, 3, 5)    exact 0.028571  rebuilt 0.028519   [indep 0.002915, pairs +0.006218, TRIPLE +0.019385]
    (3, 4, 5)    exact 0.028571  rebuilt 0.028485   [indep 0.002915, pairs +0.004519, TRIPLE +0.021051]
    (2, 5, 7)    exact 0.020408  rebuilt 0.020480   [indep 0.002915, pairs +0.001167, TRIPLE +0.016398]
    (3, 5, 8)    exact 0.017857  rebuilt 0.017828   [indep 0.002915, pairs +0.000435, TRIPLE +0.014478]

  => the genuinely 3-body term d123 is separated from the pair terms.
     Pairs are THM-965 (closed form); d123 is the new object.
(3) THE VANISHING AT MULTIPLES OF 7  [7 = 1/(2*lam)]
    hhat(n) = sin(pi n/7)/(pi n) = 0 exactly when 7 | n:
      hhat( 1) = +0.13810948   
      hhat( 2) = +0.12443235   
      hhat( 6) = +0.02301825   
      hhat( 7) = +0.00000000   <-- ZERO
      hhat( 8) = -0.01726369   
      hhat(13) = -0.01062381   
      hhat(14) = -0.00000000   <-- ZERO
      hhat(21) = +0.00000000   <-- ZERO
    => every resonance vector with ANY coordinate divisible by 7
       contributes NOTHING.  The modulus 7 is built into the transform.

