(6) EXACT-INDEPENDENCE CRITERION FROM THE LATTICE
    The pair lattice is generated by (b/g, -a/g), g = gcd(a,b).
    Every vector is s*(b/g, -a/g); it contributes only if 7 does not
    divide s*b/g AND does not divide s*a/g.  So ALL vectors die iff
            7 | (a/g)   or   7 | (b/g).
    Predicted: mu(D_a n D_b) = (2lam)^2 = 1/49 EXACTLY in that case.

    (a,b)       a/g  b/g   pred-indep   mu exact      = 1/49 ?
