(7) DILATION INVARIANCE, EXPLAINED IN ONE LINE
    Lam(k*a) = {n : sum n_i (k a_i) = 0} = {n : k * sum n_i a_i = 0} = Lam(a).
    The resonance lattice does not see the scale k at all, so every
    quantity built from it is dilation-invariant.  THM-1050 is immediate,
    and THM-1055's 'no speed threshold' follows: the lattice is an
    ARITHMETIC object and magnitude is not one of its inputs.
      mu(2, 3)     = 1/21
      mu(4, 6)     = 1/21
      mu(6, 9)     = 1/21
      mu(10, 15)   = 1/21
      mu(20, 30)   = 1/21
